From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: WavJaby <WavJaby@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 14 Nov 2026 14:33:58 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] adb: include the OpenSSL headers adb_auth.h uses

adb_auth.h declares functions taking STACK_OF(X509_NAME) but includes
only <openssl/rsa.h>. It compiles against AOSP's BoringSSL because its
ex_data.h pulls in <openssl/stack.h>; upstream BoringSSL no longer
does, so the macro is undefined. Include what the header uses.

Upstream-Status: Pending
Patch-Reason: a missing include in adb's own header; the launcher, loader or environment cannot add it, and the OpenSSL provider (upstream BoringSSL, chosen for licence reasons) is correct to omit the transitive include
---
SPDX-License-Identifier: Apache-2.0
 adb_auth.h | 2 ++
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+)

diff --git a/adb_auth.h b/adb_auth.h
index 38312211f3ade275e210e6346f905775c7611300..6ab009fd9d95b077acd89c8aae81fc9bd2dc5b05 100644
--- a/adb_auth.h
+++ b/adb_auth.h
@@ -23,6 +23,8 @@
 #include <memory>
 
 #include <openssl/rsa.h>
+#include <openssl/stack.h>
+#include <openssl/x509.h>
 
 /* AUTH packets first argument */
 /* Request */
